# NFL roster truth (BDL GOAT)

Do not assign NFL players to teams from model memory, Wikipedia, or static `api/nfl-wr-te.js` / `api/nfl-players.js` priors.

Source of truth: `api/data/nflBdlRosterSnapshot.js` (`NFL_BDL_ROSTER_SNAPSHOT.playerTeamByName`), then live `briefcase.league.rostersByTeam` / `playerTeamByName` when Ask hydrates.

Refresh with `npm run sync:nfl-bdl-rosters`.

Confirmed on the 2026 snapshot: **A.J. Brown is NE**. **Romeo Doubs is NE**. If a take, ticket review, or board filter treats them as PHI or GB, that is a bug.

# NFL props boards (BDL GOAT tier)

BDL returns thousands of props per game (alts, period markets, depth names). Best-props boards must only ship **GOAT-tier** tickets:

- Live BDL/GOAT prop rows for the featured matchup (not invented names/lines)
- Roster-scoped to the matchup via BDL roster truth
- Featured usage / half-point skill mains — not KR/depth integer alts (e.g. Vaki over 40)

Sione Vaki is a real DET roster player — still not a default best-board seat without featured usage.
